d 'ODA': module for conducting Optimal Discriminant Analysis (Windows only)
d
d  Optimal discriminant analysis is a machine learning algorithm
d that was introduced over 30 years ago to offer an alternative
d analytic approach to conventional statistical methods commonly
d used in research (Yarnold & Soltysik 1991). Its appeal lies in
d its simplicity, flexibility and accuracy as compared with
d conventional statistical methods (Yarnold & Soltysik 2005, 2016).
d Given classvar (2 or more distinct levels) and attrvar
d (continuous, or categorical via cat), oda performs an exhaustive
d search for the cutpoint, the optimal category grouping, the
d optimal ordered segmentation, or the optimal per-category class
d assignment that maximizes classification accuracy, and reports
d overall accuracy, PAC (Percent Accuracy in Classification) and PV
d (Predictive Value) for every class, and their corresponding
d Effect Strength (ESS) measures. oda extends ODA's original
d functionality in a number of ways -- most notably bootstrap
d confidence intervals and a significance test on the leave-one-out
d table for a multi-category classvar (looreps()). 
d
d KW: machine learning
d KW: data mining
d KW: Discriminant analysis
d KW: Classification analysis
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 for Windows and purchase of ODA software 
d
d Distribution-Date: 20200909
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
